// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1, part (a) (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P8): a global text aliased into a global
// record's text field. Originally (4e): the select-LHS store rule
// disqualified only the FIELD NAME on a non-fresh store, never the
// record's own base -- `cl_free_globals` still recursed into `p8GRec`'s
// fields, freeing `body` (== `p8Gt`'s handle, after the store), then
// separately froze `p8Gt` itself: SIGSEGV. The fix disqualifies the BASE
// identifier (`p8GRec`) too, so `cl_free_globals` stayed empty for it
// through ARC Task 5, skipping `p8GRec` entirely.
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p8GRec.body = p8Gt` is a
// SELECT-LHS store -- `lowAssign`'s generic fallthrough doesn't
// distinguish a record field from a window var, so this ALSO routes
// through `lowCountedStore` (an early, incidental win Task 7's record
// copy-site work will formalize, not a bug: retaining a field store can
// only ever be a leak if unbalanced, never a UAF). Confirmed against the
// emitted C: `rt_text_retain(cv_p8Gt); rt_text_release((cv_p8GRec).cv_body);
// (cv_p8GRec).cv_body = cv_p8Gt;` -- `p8ProbeNote`'s original `body = "hi"`
// default handle is properly freed now (no longer the permanent
// orphan-on-overwrite this comment used to describe), and `p8Gt` is
// retained into the field.
//
// ARC Task 6 (globals release unconditionally) drops the `p8GRec`
// disqualification: `cl_free_globals` now walks EVERY global, including
// `p8GRec`, via `cpEmitRelease`'s existing (pre-ARC) KRec case, which
// already recurses into every needs-ctor field unconditionally -- that
// per-field walk was never gated, only the TOP-LEVEL `p8GRec` slot was.
// `p8Gt` (declared first) is also no longer disqualified, so both release:
// declaration order releases `p8Gt`'s own handle first (rc==2 -> 1), then
// `p8GRec`'s field walk releases the SAME handle via `body` (rc==1 -> 0,
// freed). Expected strict-mode leak count: 0 (../p8_rec_field.leaks
// deleted -- was 2). Safe: `p8Gt`'s retain-at-store (Task 4) gave the
// shared "keep" text its own independent +1, so the two releases are
// draining that rc==2 back to 0, not double-freeing. A record copy site
// (whole-record assignment/param/return/element -- Task 7's scope, not
// exercised by this fixture) is a separate, still-open question.

record p8ProbeNote {
    body: text = "hi"
}

var p8Gt: text = "keep"
var p8GRec: p8ProbeNote

func runP8RecField() {
    p8GRec.body = p8Gt
    alert("p8 done")
}
